error[V0204]: this `match` does not handle every number; end it with a catch-all arm, `_ => ...`
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0204_number_without_catch_all/main.vr:2:5
  |
2 |     match n {
  |     ^^^^^^^ this `match` does not handle every number; end it with a catch-all arm, `_ => ...`
  |
  = note: Varyk counts every number and every string as having more values than arms can list, so a `match` on one always ends with a catch-all; in Rust terms, the patterns are not exhaustive
